Description: Write and Tables closer to the design boards
 Follows the ribbon, style cards and Tables chrome patches.
 The ribbon's group labels are quiet again: the pages are filled after the
 tab control first shows, so the labels are styled whenever the ribbon
 paints. File and Find a command use the tab row's own font, which is in
 pixels (the style's tab font is in points and drew them small). In dark
 mode the tab row is the window colour, so it runs on from the title bar
 rather than making a darker stripe under it.
 Colour buttons in a toolbox with wildos-no-arrows show their icon as
 drawn, the red A and the amber marker on the boards, without the bar of
 the current colour.
 The style gallery keeps its cards 6 px apart. An icon view widens its
 entries to each new image plus 5 px either side, which spread the cards
 10 px apart and pushed the last one past the gallery's edge.
 Font sizes read as plain points ("11"); "11 pt" typed in still works.
 The sidebar's strip holds only its decks, without the settings button,
 and split window edges are a hairline with a quiet arrow for the fade
 button instead of a grey rule and a white block.
Author: Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>
Forwarded: not-needed
